From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: raise the CLI schema subprocess timeout to 300s

test_schema_parity_structural and test_schema_parity_samples both go
through _cli_schema(), which shells out to `cargo run --release -p
wolfxl-cli -- schema ... --format json` with a hardcoded
subprocess.run(timeout=120). On riscv64 that `cargo run` is the first
invocation that touches the wolfxl-cli binary crate in the whole test
job: the build job only builds the cdylib extension via `maturin
build`, which doesn't share a target directory with a bare `cargo
run` on the runner, so this is a first-time release compile of
wolfxl-cli and its dependency graph, not just a process launch.

Upstream's own CI (test-python in .github/workflows/ci.yml) doesn't
pre-build wolfxl-cli either; it stays under 120s there because
RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache with SCCACHE_GHA_ENABLED=true gives it a warm,
cross-run object-code cache. Our riscv64 runner has no sccache, and
is slower per-core than the x86_64 GitHub-hosted runners this bound
was tuned against, so the same cold compile overruns 120s and both
tests fail with subprocess.TimeoutExpired, independent of pytest-xdist
worker count (confirmed: 3677 other tests pass, only these two
cargo-invoking tests time out).

120s was sized for "process is already built, just run it" on fast,
cache-warmed hardware -- it was never a statement about how long a
release compile of wolfxl-cli should take. Raise it to 300s so a cold
compile on slower/uncached hardware has room, while a hung or
genuinely broken `cargo run` still fails loudly well within pytest's
own job timeout.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64 CI has no sccache cache to warm the cold `cargo run -p wolfxl-cli` compile that 120s assumed away; not a defect in wolfxl itself]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/tests/test_classifier_parity.py b/tests/test_classifier_parity.py
index ca0d45b..b3c6465 100644
--- a/tests/test_classifier_parity.py
+++ b/tests/test_classifier_parity.py
@@ -89,7 +89,11 @@ def _cli_schema(path: Path) -> dict:
         capture_output=True,
         text=True,
         cwd=REPO_ROOT,
-        timeout=120,
+        # 120s assumes wolfxl-cli is already built; on riscv64 CI (no sccache,
+        # slower per-core than upstream's x86_64 runners) this is the first
+        # `cargo run` to touch the binary crate, so it includes a cold release
+        # compile. Widen the bound rather than the test's intent.
+        timeout=300,
         env={**dict(os.environ), "CARGO_TERM_COLOR": "never"},
     )
     assert result.returncode == 0, (
--
2.43.0
